  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pathways to Prosperity - Linking and Learning Latin America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of our broader programmatic Linking and Learning strategy in the Pathways to Prosperity programme, specifically supporting the region.
The project has two main objectives:
1. To assess the impact of the EUDR on the smallholder coffee sectors in Mesoamerica and co-develop solutions to support the sector to comply with the regulation towards a more sustainable and traceable coffee sector.   
2.  Conducting a financial cost-benefit analysis of the existing Payment for ecosystem services models (ACORN projects)  to provide recommendations and identify opportunities for cost efficiencies to increase the value proposition of Solidaridad-led ACORN projects in Latin America.
The insights gained will contribute to scale mechanisms that support smallholder farmers to meet market requirements and access sustainable markets. Also, will contribute to allow buyers to get sustainable and inclusive products and pay for ecosystem services.</narrative>
  </description>
